`snapshot diff` is the offline half of the `.zsnap` verb (#219, RFC 13 §4.4):
two files in, no session, and the one contract the section makes
non-negotiable — **both spans stated**, in the envelope and in the caveat —
visible on every exit code. The fixtures are the shared report fixtures
written through the engine's own writer (`tests/render.rs` keeps them in
step), so this case and the render snapshots read the same bytes.

Rows line up by their **zk2 key** (#612, FJ8b): the namespace is stripped on
both sides, so a deployment compares to another deployment with no origin
alignment to ask for — the key already names the system and the service.

**1 — they differ.** A difference *is* the finding. Every row is tagged by
kind (`added`, `removed`, `changed`), and a `changed` row carries only the
facets that moved: `eth0`'s value *and* its conformance (it was fixed), and
`host-b/tc`'s holder (an address no instance held came back).

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/b.zsnap
? 1
{"a":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["acme/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":2},"b":{"answered":4,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-10-09T00:05:00Z","collection_span_s":0.8,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["acme/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"zsnap":2},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.80s at 2026-10-09T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":1}
{"key":"zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/interfaces/default/eth1","row":"added"}
{"key":"zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/interfaces/default/eth9","row":"removed"}
{"conformance":[{"state":"invalid","violations":["/is_up: expected boolean"]},{"state":"valid"}],"key":"zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/interfaces/default/eth0","row":"changed","timestamp":["7f3b2a1c00000001/ab12","7f3b2a1c00000002/ab12"],"value":{"changes":[{"new":true,"old":"yes","op":"changed","path":"is_up"}],"truncated":0}}
{"holder":[{"address":"host-b/tc","kind":"no_instance"},{"address":"host-b/tc","answered_by":"owner","kind":"live"}],"key":"zk2/host-b/tc/tc.netif.v1/state/namespaces","row":"changed","timestamp":["7f3b2a1c00000001/cd34","7f3b2a1c00000001/cd34"]}
a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.80s at 2026-10-09T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)

```

**0 — identical on every facet.** The clean answer, with the spans still
stated: an empty diff is a statement about two collections, not about an
instant.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap
{"a":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["acme/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":2},"b":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["acme/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":2},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":4}
a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)

```

Two namespaces, one diff: `staging.zsnap` is the same deployment under
`staging`, an hour on, on another clock. The keys line up, and the two
deployments' clocks are not compared — a stamp that moved alone is not a
change, and the caveat says so.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/staging.zsnap
{"a":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["acme/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":2},"b":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"staging","collected_at":"2026-10-09T01:00:00Z","collection_span_s":0.9,"presence":{"complete":true,"selector":"zk2/*/*/@zk/**","services":2},"selectors":["staging/zk2/*/*/*/state/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":2},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.90s at 2026-10-09T01:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"},{"cite":"spec §1.6","text":"keys compared relative to each file's namespace (a: /"acme/", b: /"staging/"); two deployments' clocks are not compared, so a stamp that moved alone is not a change here"}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":4}
a: span 1.25s at 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.90s at 2026-10-09T01:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)
keys compared relative to each file's namespace (a: "acme", b: "staging"); two deployments' clocks are not compared, so a stamp that moved alone is not a change here (spec §1.6)

```

**2 — the question could not be asked.** A file that will not read is the
reserved non-verdict, never a 1 claiming the two differ — the same split
`check schema` guards.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/missing.zsnap
? 2
Error: open tests/cmd/fixtures/missing.zsnap

Caused by:
    No such file or directory (os error 2)
snapshot diff: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A v1 `.zsnap` is refused the same way, with a hint: its keys are v1's, and
there is nothing to line them up with.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/v1.zsnap
? 2
Error: read tests/cmd/fixtures/v1.zsnap

Caused by:
    .zsnap: unsupported version 1 (this reader speaks 2) — a version-1 file is v1's registry snapshot, which the `v1` branch reads
snapshot diff: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
